AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_4f2d3939_91b1_4001_b8ab_7d19074bf845> "ElectricPotential"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> <https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_4f2d3939_91b1_4001_b8ab_7d19074bf845> "Electric potential is the amount of electric potential energy per unit charge at a specific point in an electric field. In electrochemistry, it helps describe the energy state of an electrode relative to a reference electrode. It is a fundamental concept in electrode reactions, influencing redox potential and determining the driving force behind electrochemical processes. Electric potential is commonly measured in volts (V) and is essential for understanding electrode kinetics, corrosion processes, and electrochemical equilibrium."@en)
